1
00:00:03,267 --> 00:00:04,767
He's mine.

2
00:00:04,967 --> 00:00:06,600
Don't flatter yourself.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:07,933
Huh?

4
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,167
Oh! Wait... wait!

5
00:00:13,067 --> 00:00:15,067
You always just play it off and run away.

6
00:00:15,767 --> 00:00:18,000
If you hate me, just say it!

7
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,567
I don't hate you!

8
00:00:20,967 --> 00:00:22,933
It's not like I hate you...

9
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:28,867
Ah... no, well...

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:30,700
Takoi-san.

11
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,967
Yes?

12
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,267
I like you.

13
00:00:40,533 --> 00:00:42,533
How did this happen...

14
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,467
So I...

15
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:47,500
I don't actually hate Shiono.

16
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:53,100
Ah...

17
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:57,367
We're closed.

18
00:00:57,467 --> 00:00:58,833
Oh...

19
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,733
What happened?

20
00:01:38,533 --> 00:01:40,500
What on earth is going on?

21
00:02:12,833 --> 00:02:15,767
"Duty First, Kiss Later"

22
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:20,633
(Episode 3)

23
00:02:32,167 --> 00:02:33,633
Good morning.

24
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:35,800
You scared me.

25
00:02:36,267 --> 00:02:38,367
I came over because you looked so down.

26
00:02:39,567 --> 00:02:41,033
Are you okay?

27
00:02:41,633 --> 00:02:42,953
Do I look like something's wrong?

28
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:44,800
You don't look so good.

29
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:46,267
Hungover?

30
00:02:47,367 --> 00:02:48,667
You could say that.

31
00:02:48,767 --> 00:02:50,067
That's rare for you.

32
00:02:50,167 --> 00:02:51,767
Did something happen?

33
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:55,800
Is it about Shiono?

34
00:02:56,333 --> 00:02:57,767
Yeah.

35
00:02:58,467 --> 00:03:00,633
Wait, how did you know?

36
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:03,867
It's obvious.

37
00:03:17,167 --> 00:03:19,567
(Yama-no-michi Police Station)

38
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:23,967
Takoi.

39
00:03:24,333 --> 00:03:26,900
This is for you from Yamada-san.

40
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,500
Which one?

41
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:29,800
What do you mean, which one?

42
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,700
The old man?

43
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:38,999
"I apologize for my ignorance of your situation.
I wish you happiness always. - Yamada"

44
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,900
I apologize for my
ignorance of your situation.

45
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:45,433
I wish you happiness.

46
00:03:46,433 --> 00:03:47,867
Ugh...

47
00:03:47,967 --> 00:03:49,267
What is this?

48
00:03:50,733 --> 00:03:53,800
I apologize for my
ignorance of your situation...

49
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:55,000
Hey.

50
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,500
Yeah.

51
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,000
Oh.

52
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:00,100
So it's grapes.

53
00:04:00,167 --> 00:04:01,500
Time to dig in.

54
00:04:02,967 --> 00:04:04,767
So sweet. They're delicious.

55
00:04:11,333 --> 00:04:12,643
Heading out for questioning.

56
00:04:12,667 --> 00:04:14,367
- Take care.
- Take care.

57
00:04:20,267 --> 00:04:21,633
I'm heading out!

58
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,433
Hey, Shiono.

59
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:41,433
(Yama-no-michi Police Station)

60
00:04:46,233 --> 00:04:47,800
I won't come looking for you again.

61
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:49,867
Please don't tell anyone about this.

62
00:04:49,967 --> 00:04:51,267
Huh?

63
00:04:51,633 --> 00:04:52,867
Goodbye.

64
00:04:52,967 --> 00:04:54,000
What?

65
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,833
Didn't you already tell the old man?

66
00:04:58,967 --> 00:05:00,300
What are you doing?

67
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:03,233
You're on the clock, right?

68
00:05:05,667 --> 00:05:06,233
Takoi-san.

69
00:05:06,333 --> 00:05:07,633
Don't follow me.

70
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:10,653
- Where I need to go is right there.
- Didn't I tell you not to follow me?

71
00:05:10,767 --> 00:05:12,167
Um...

72
00:05:14,033 --> 00:05:15,433
I wanted to talk about yesterday...

73
00:05:38,067 --> 00:05:40,300
Why am I always running?

74
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:50,267
That girl, I remember...

75
00:05:57,833 --> 00:05:59,000
Hikari-chan.

76
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:04,500
I'm Takoi. We met at the
Yama-no-michi Police Station.

77
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,000
Do you remember me?

78
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:10,900
Why aren't you at school?

79
00:06:12,833 --> 00:06:16,267
My stomach hurts just
thinking about going to school.

80
00:06:19,367 --> 00:06:20,867
I see.

81
00:06:20,967 --> 00:06:22,600
Can you get to school by yourself?

82
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:25,400
Yes.

83
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:26,633
Okay.

84
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,300
Ah.

85
00:06:32,133 --> 00:06:33,333
Here, take this.

86
00:06:37,167 --> 00:06:40,567
If anything happens,
can you call this number?

87
00:06:44,033 --> 00:06:46,133
I'll help you anytime you need it.

88
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:51,376
"Sergeant Takoi Heisuke Chief of Criminal
Affairs, Saitama Yama-no-michi Police Station"

89
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:54,433
I'm Takoi Heisuke.

90
00:06:56,433 --> 00:06:57,067
Thank you.

91
00:07:00,667 --> 00:07:01,967
Be careful not to trip.

92
00:07:16,067 --> 00:07:19,100
She must be devastated.

93
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,333
Yeah.

94
00:07:20,433 --> 00:07:24,400
Her dad had an affair and got into
a fight with the woman's husband.

95
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:26,933
He ended up hitting him and got arrested.

96
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:29,233
What a piece of trash.

97
00:07:31,433 --> 00:07:32,167
I'm stuffed.

98
00:07:32,267 --> 00:07:34,700
Wow, you ate way too fast, didn't you?

99
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:36,643
We have a crime prevention
campaign this afternoon.

100
00:07:36,667 --> 00:07:38,609
The higher-ups want the Criminal
Affairs Division to attend too.

101
00:07:38,633 --> 00:07:40,233
Whoa, is it that time already?

102
00:07:40,333 --> 00:07:41,333
Yeah.

103
00:07:41,433 --> 00:07:44,367
At least we get to enjoy
a relaxing lunch, Takoi.

104
00:07:45,067 --> 00:07:47,667
Don't jinx it,
or we'll be swamped today.

105
00:07:47,767 --> 00:07:49,467
That happens way too often.

106
00:07:49,567 --> 00:07:50,033
Alright.

107
00:07:50,133 --> 00:07:52,267
Please, let nothing go wrong today.

108
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:53,967
Okay.
Alright, let's go.

109
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:55,333
Yes, sir.

110
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:57,000
- Take care.
- We're heading out!

111
00:07:59,933 --> 00:08:01,933
So sweet!

112
00:08:02,467 --> 00:08:03,767
You can have some more.

113
00:08:04,833 --> 00:08:06,967
No one's delivering bento boxes anymore.

114
00:08:07,067 --> 00:08:08,767
Takoi Heisuke.

115
00:08:09,433 --> 00:08:12,700
But no one will be delivering
them in the future either.

116
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:15,600
It ended before it even began.

117
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:17,533
I have my own issues to deal with.

118
00:08:17,633 --> 00:08:20,967
At this rate, you'll be
living in the dorms forever.

119
00:08:21,267 --> 00:08:22,500
With Shiono.

120
00:08:26,433 --> 00:08:27,133
Here.

121
00:08:27,233 --> 00:08:28,300
Sorry.

122
00:08:35,267 --> 00:08:36,167
Say.

123
00:08:36,267 --> 00:08:37,267
Hmm?

124
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:38,167
Hypothetically speaking.
Yeah.

125
00:08:38,867 --> 00:08:41,767
Let's say you're single
right now, Hasegawa.

126
00:08:41,867 --> 00:08:42,633
Okay.

127
00:08:42,733 --> 00:08:45,767
And there's someone you think
you could absolutely never date.

128
00:08:45,867 --> 00:08:48,633
If they confessed their feelings
to you, what would you do?

129
00:08:51,067 --> 00:08:52,267
Hey.

130
00:08:55,833 --> 00:08:58,967
You shouldn't ask a married
man a question like that.

131
00:08:59,067 --> 00:09:01,967
I'm just speaking hypothetically.

132
00:09:02,067 --> 00:09:04,700
If it were me...

133
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:06,800
I'd give dating them a shot.

134
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:07,933
Give it a shot?

135
00:09:08,033 --> 00:09:10,367
Can you really say it's
absolutely impossible?

136
00:09:11,167 --> 00:09:12,800
You haven't even dated them yet, right?

137
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,600
But they must have braced themselves,

138
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,500
prepared for rejection,

139
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,367
and gathered the courage
to confess to you, right?

140
00:09:24,233 --> 00:09:28,767
Doesn't that make
your heart flutter a little?

141
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,900
Aren't you a little too old
for your heart to be fluttering?

142
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:39,300
(Incoming Call: Misuzu Mama)

143
00:09:42,267 --> 00:09:43,767
Hey, Mama, what's wrong?

144
00:09:47,967 --> 00:09:49,967
Are you kidding me?! You bastard!

145
00:09:50,067 --> 00:09:51,633
I'm a cop!

146
00:09:53,033 --> 00:09:54,400
Takoi.

147
00:09:58,900 --> 00:10:00,667
You dared to call the cops?

148
00:10:00,691 --> 00:10:01,991
Damn right I did.

149
00:10:02,167 --> 00:10:04,400
Was I supposed to just
watch you kill someone?

150
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:05,767
This is all your fault!

151
00:10:05,867 --> 00:10:07,400
Always hanging all over that guy!

152
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:08,800
We can talk about this later.

153
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:10,433
Let go of me!

154
00:10:10,533 --> 00:10:11,267
Calm down.

155
00:10:11,367 --> 00:10:12,700
Let go!

156
00:10:13,633 --> 00:10:14,733
Don't do anything stupid.

157
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:16,133
Move.

158
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:17,967
Let's go.

159
00:10:22,867 --> 00:10:24,367
Behave yourself.

160
00:10:27,667 --> 00:10:29,367
Misuzu.

161
00:10:29,833 --> 00:10:32,167
We've been over for a long time!

162
00:10:32,867 --> 00:10:34,100
Besides...

163
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:38,200
I've been really busy lately.

164
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:39,533
Don't ever come back.

165
00:10:39,633 --> 00:10:40,833
Huh?

166
00:10:43,367 --> 00:10:44,867
Misuzu...

167
00:10:45,833 --> 00:10:48,967
Keep protecting me from now on, Takoi.

168
00:10:49,067 --> 00:10:51,133
No... wait a minute, Mama.

169
00:10:55,733 --> 00:10:57,600
Don't look down on me!

170
00:11:46,133 --> 00:11:47,000
Cuff him.

171
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:48,233
Let's go!

172
00:11:52,133 --> 00:11:54,800
Are... are you okay?

173
00:11:57,633 --> 00:11:58,800
You're bleeding.

174
00:11:58,900 --> 00:11:59,567
It's fine.

175
00:11:59,667 --> 00:12:00,800
But...

176
00:12:02,333 --> 00:12:05,533
I'll leave the rest to you guys.

177
00:12:08,733 --> 00:12:09,733
Are you alright?

178
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,367
You'd better go to the hospital.

179
00:12:16,533 --> 00:12:17,667
Takoi...?

180
00:12:37,967 --> 00:12:40,233
Ah, where's Shiono?

181
00:12:40,333 --> 00:12:42,267
I heard he was hospitalized.

182
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:44,333
Seriously?

183
00:12:44,433 --> 00:12:45,433
Yes.

184
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:48,900
He took a pretty hard
hit to the head, after all.

185
00:12:49,333 --> 00:12:50,633
It's all my fault.

186
00:12:53,233 --> 00:12:55,767
I just heard Shiono was discharged.

187
00:12:55,867 --> 00:12:56,533
Huh?

188
00:12:56,633 --> 00:12:57,667
Really?

189
00:12:57,767 --> 00:12:59,267
Yeah.

190
00:13:00,767 --> 00:13:02,467
Thank goodness!

191
00:13:07,533 --> 00:13:10,767
Do you want to go check on him?

192
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:46,933
What are you doing?

193
00:13:47,233 --> 00:13:48,633
Ah... nothing.

194
00:13:49,233 --> 00:13:50,776
Since you're here, come on in for a bit.

195
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:51,567
Huh?

196
00:13:51,667 --> 00:13:54,133
Come in, hurry up and come in.

197
00:13:59,033 --> 00:14:01,100
Not drinking today?

198
00:14:01,467 --> 00:14:03,200
Yeah, not today.

199
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,067
What about the bar?

200
00:14:07,167 --> 00:14:08,567
Are you taking a break for a while?

201
00:14:08,633 --> 00:14:11,333
No way, I'm reopening right away.

202
00:14:11,433 --> 00:14:14,433
Otherwise, my regulars
won't have a place to drink.

203
00:14:14,733 --> 00:14:16,033
Spoken like a true Mama.

204
00:14:17,767 --> 00:14:20,600
I'm going to make that
guy pay for everything.

205
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:28,467
By the way, [that other guy's]
name is Shiono-san, right?

206
00:14:28,567 --> 00:14:30,167
He's really handsome.

207
00:14:30,567 --> 00:14:31,967
Is he your partner?

208
00:14:32,733 --> 00:14:33,633
No, he's not.

209
00:14:33,733 --> 00:14:35,767
We're not even in the same department.

210
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:37,800
Really?

211
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:40,167
But, how should I put it...

212
00:14:40,267 --> 00:14:44,367
He's a really charming guy.

213
00:14:46,467 --> 00:14:47,867
Yeah.

214
00:14:48,333 --> 00:14:50,300
I thought he was cold at first.

215
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:53,067
I didn't expect him to
step up and protect Takoi.

216
00:14:53,167 --> 00:14:54,700
He's exactly my type.

217
00:14:59,733 --> 00:15:04,633
By the way, who is this box for?

218
00:15:05,567 --> 00:15:06,800
I'm going to eat it myself.

219
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:08,300
Yeah, right.

220
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:09,400
Huh?

221
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:13,233
Takoyaki is meant to be eaten hot.

222
00:15:13,333 --> 00:15:15,800
But you haven't touched it.

223
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:19,900
And it doesn't look like
you're going to offer me any.

224
00:15:20,633 --> 00:15:27,100
So, it must be for someone else.

225
00:15:29,033 --> 00:15:30,400
Are you a detective or something?

226
00:15:30,967 --> 00:15:34,133
Don't underestimate a bar
Mama's observation skills.

227
00:15:38,733 --> 00:15:40,133
Hurry up and deliver it.

228
00:15:46,167 --> 00:15:47,933
It won't taste good if you wait too long.

229
00:15:48,033 --> 00:15:49,267
It's the same with everything.

230
00:15:49,367 --> 00:15:52,067
You have to strike while the iron is hot.

231
00:15:52,667 --> 00:15:54,567
Strike while the iron is hot.

232
00:15:56,867 --> 00:15:58,067
Right?

233
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:08,700
Thanks for the treat.

234
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:10,200
Thank you, Mama.

235
00:16:12,933 --> 00:16:15,133
Let me know if you ever need anything.

236
00:16:15,233 --> 00:16:16,833
I'll take you up on that.

237
00:16:16,933 --> 00:16:18,333
Go on, hurry up.

238
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,833
Ouch! That hurts!

239
00:16:45,867 --> 00:16:47,433
What are you doing?

240
00:16:49,433 --> 00:16:51,000
Are you okay?

241
00:16:52,133 --> 00:16:53,367
Yeah.

242
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,900
I came to check on you.

243
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,640
I figured you must be having a hard time.

244
00:17:01,067 --> 00:17:02,500
Thank you.

245
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,500
I was just heading out to buy some things.

246
00:17:05,367 --> 00:17:06,667
Oh.

247
00:17:09,433 --> 00:17:10,667
Huh?

248
00:17:15,767 --> 00:17:19,567
Your injury must be pretty bad, right?

249
00:17:19,933 --> 00:17:23,600
It's fine, it's actually nothing serious.

250
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,567
I'll wash it.

251
00:17:25,667 --> 00:17:27,033
Huh?

252
00:17:38,733 --> 00:17:40,700
Can I have some takoyaki?

253
00:17:42,267 --> 00:17:43,500
It's already cold.

254
00:17:47,667 --> 00:17:50,200
You don't need to worry about me.

255
00:17:51,033 --> 00:17:52,873
A little ointment and
I'll be fine in no time.

256
00:17:52,933 --> 00:17:54,900
The brain scan came back clear too.

257
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:57,100
Yeah.

258
00:18:05,133 --> 00:18:06,800
Do you think it's all your fault?

259
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,700
Yeah.

260
00:18:12,833 --> 00:18:14,200
It's my fault.

261
00:18:19,533 --> 00:18:21,333
It's exactly like you said.

262
00:18:23,167 --> 00:18:25,367
I was being too nosy.

263
00:18:25,933 --> 00:18:27,900
And I ended up getting someone hurt.

264
00:18:37,333 --> 00:18:39,333
Misuzu-san came to
visit me at the hospital.

265
00:18:39,433 --> 00:18:41,467
Huh, Mama?

266
00:18:42,167 --> 00:18:44,533
She kept apologizing to me.

267
00:18:44,633 --> 00:18:46,833
Saying it was all her fault
things turned out this way.

268
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:53,200
Then she just kept talking about Takoi-san.

269
00:18:53,967 --> 00:18:56,447
She couldn't stop singing
Takoi-san's praises before she left.

270
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:58,367
I really don't know why she even came.

271
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:03,700
You're so gentle with everyone.

272
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:06,933
Always giving people the wrong idea.

273
00:19:08,433 --> 00:19:11,433
If it were me, I'd be really pissed off.

274
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:16,833
But you've also helped a
lot of people because of it.

275
00:19:17,433 --> 00:19:19,467
Because that's just who Takoi-san is.

276
00:19:19,567 --> 00:19:22,367
Isn't that a good thing?

277
00:19:25,167 --> 00:19:27,033
I don't find it funny.

278
00:19:27,133 --> 00:19:28,967
Now I have even more competition.

279
00:19:31,633 --> 00:19:33,233
Thank you.

280
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:41,733
Okay.

281
00:19:42,167 --> 00:19:43,667
All clean.

282
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:48,033
That's great.

283
00:19:52,567 --> 00:19:53,567
Huh?

284
00:19:55,467 --> 00:19:56,733
What?

285
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:58,933
Are you blushing?

286
00:20:03,667 --> 00:20:05,667
It's actually been bothering me.

287
00:20:06,267 --> 00:20:07,933
Is that so...

288
00:20:08,567 --> 00:20:09,867
Well...

289
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:16,600
I thought you hated me.

290
00:20:17,567 --> 00:20:18,900
Why?

291
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,567
Did I do something?

292
00:20:20,667 --> 00:20:22,187
Weren't you always saying mean things?

293
00:20:22,867 --> 00:20:24,233
And...

294
00:20:24,767 --> 00:20:27,600
No matter what I did,
you always got in my way.

295
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:30,200
And you always looked down on me.

296
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:33,300
Plus, you were especially cold to me.

297
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:35,633
Because...

298
00:20:36,333 --> 00:20:38,100
I was just really annoyed.

299
00:20:40,033 --> 00:20:41,433
Huh?

300
00:20:43,233 --> 00:20:46,133
I know Takoi-san likes women.

301
00:20:48,133 --> 00:20:49,333
No matter what,

302
00:20:49,433 --> 00:20:51,800
I could never be an option for you.

303
00:20:55,167 --> 00:20:56,600
So...

304
00:20:58,167 --> 00:20:59,700
I was just frustrated.

305
00:21:07,367 --> 00:21:09,300
I wanted you to notice me.

306
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:14,400
Even though I don't
think we could ever date,

307
00:21:21,433 --> 00:21:23,333
I just wanted to tell you.

308
00:21:23,433 --> 00:21:25,200
I like you.

309
00:21:30,700 --> 00:21:32,033
I'm sorry.

310
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:41,780
You have something on your head.

311
00:21:41,833 --> 00:21:43,067
Huh?

312
00:21:44,967 --> 00:21:46,467
What is it?

313
00:21:47,133 --> 00:21:49,600
Cabbage. Kamekichi's food.

314
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:51,733
That's hilarious.

315
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:55,467
How did you even get that on your head?

316
00:22:24,833 --> 00:22:27,533
(This drama is purely fictional.)

317
00:22:28,033 --> 00:22:29,933
(Next Episode)

318
00:22:30,033 --> 00:22:31,033
You should head back too.

319
00:22:31,067 --> 00:22:34,200
I'm going to arrest you.

320
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:36,633
I wanted to be alone with you.

321
00:22:36,733 --> 00:22:38,400
What do we do now?

322
00:22:38,933 --> 00:22:40,109
If I go back and hurt him again...

323
00:22:40,133 --> 00:22:40,867
Shut up.

324
00:22:40,967 --> 00:22:43,067
I hate Takoi-san the most.

325
00:22:45,767 --> 00:22:46,600
Takoi-san...

326
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:48,233
Can you take responsibility for this?
